## 2. Inherited Phase 1.5 execution constitution

{% mermaid_diagram src="/diagrams/mermaid/phase-1-6-execution-constitution.mmd" title="Inherited Phase 1.5 execution constitution" /%}
*Figure 2. Phase 1.6 creates knowledge and authority packages; frozen Phase 1.5 performs controlled execution.*

### 2.1 Capabilities inherited unchanged

| Inherited capability | Phase 1.6 rule |
|---|---|
| Eight agent roles | Reuse the fixed role set; do not create a parallel research execution workforce. |
| Context compiler | Extend inputs/references where needed; do not rebuild provider-specific prompt assembly. |
| Claude/Codex provider boundary | Reuse provider-neutral routing, capacity status and continuation state. |
| Token auditor and budgets | Use existing budget controls for Phase 1.6 work packages. **Exception (V5): any inherited mechanism reading a cached/static file for gate, capacity, or deployment state must comply with the revalidation rule in Section 29A before Phase 1.6 relies on it — tracked as Phase 1.5 closure-hardening, not new Phase 1.6 scope.** |
| Tool policy / risk / council | Research does not bypass pre-tool or review authority. |
| Publication readiness | All Phase 1.6 PRs inherit localReady/publicationReady/external evidence discipline. |
| CI / attestation / promotion / rollback | No alternate Phase 1.6 delivery pipeline. |

### 2.2 What Phase 1.6 owns

- Thought capture and knowledge classification
- Research Threads and Question Trees
- Source/Evidence/Claim lineage
- UnderstandingVersions and Understanding Packages
- Visual/interactive learning compilation
- Decision Readiness and Decision Candidates
- ADR request preparation and architecture/documentation impact calculation
- Knowledge/outcome feedback and public/private projections
- **Capacity Watcher: predictive provider-usage monitoring and automatic handoff
  triggering** *(new in V5 — see Section 29A)*

